The time is past half past six on Thursday evening.
Our badminton game just finished.
Kiran, Sara, and I played well together.
All three of us are sweating a lot.
Kiran and Sara put their rackets in their bags, and I returned my rented racket at the desk.
We wiped our faces with a towel.
The month is April.
So it is very warm in the evening.
"Maya, are you very tired today?" Sara asks.
I laughed.
"Yes, I am a bit tired," I said.
Kiran says, "We played fast today."
We sit there quietly for some time.
